CFMelder traversal order

- RegionMelder aligns mapped block pairs in function order. DenseMap bucket order
  otherwise changes the order in which aligned blocks are emitted and named.
- RegionReplicator keeps discovery order for CFG work and for the mapping used
  to attach edges. The worklist used to switch to pointer order above its inline
  capacity, and the mapping affected predecessor use-list order and concretization.
- RegionReplicator processes PHI work in insertion order, including above the
  inline capacity. It visits dominance-frontier blocks in function order instead
  of walking the pointer-ordered set, preserving PHI placement and SSA rules.

